  ✓ Stage 2: check program fidelity, trusted translation, and differential behavior
  ✓ Stage 3: reconstruct all definitions and rerun every positive proof claim
  ✓ Stage 4: audit claim adequacy and real-program pinning with satisfying witnesses
  ✓ Stage 5: inventory and review every syntax/function/rule/attribute for soundness
  ✓ Stage 6: build and run a fresh meaningful false mutation
  → Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed facts and write REVIEW.md verdict
